And as I was moving towards it

00:45:01.920 --> 00:45:05.360
and...and the heretics in those caves were probably

00:45:05.360 --> 00:45:08.000
right on top of the play as far as that goes

00:45:08.000 --> 00:45:10.700
and so they had everything distorted in their mind

00:45:10.700 --> 00:45:13.040
and for some reason this psychological thing

00:45:13.040 --> 00:45:15.160
brings up old memories.

00:45:15.400 --> 00:45:19.240
And maybe it's a factor that they're all so devout anyway.

00:45:19.780 --> 00:45:21.240
They were devout anyway.

00:45:21.240 --> 00:45:25.860
So their beliefs were amplified so hard, and their guilt and their shame

00:45:25.860 --> 00:45:30.240
and their, quote-unquote, "sin" was amplified to an extreme degree.

00:45:30.240 --> 00:45:31.840
Like, they were already a cult!

00:45:32.380 --> 00:45:34.980
Like, they were already a cult.  Let's give them that.

00:45:34.980 --> 00:45:38.780
They were already in this belief system when they got there.

00:45:38.980 --> 00:45:41.480
Things started coming to reality because

00:45:41.480 --> 00:45:44.560
of the experimentation that must have been happening to them.

00:45:44.760 --> 00:45:46.620
That...HAS to be it!

00:45:47.280 --> 00:45:49.040
There is no other explanation.

00:45:49.040 --> 00:45:52.340
Why didn't you explain anything?!

00:45:52.960 --> 00:45:56.400
The sun didn't blow up and kill everybody!

00:45:56.820 --> 00:45:58.940
I'm willing to bet that!

00:46:00.060 --> 00:46:02.780
There's no way!

00:46:03.140 --> 00:46:04.900
[angry Markiplier noises]

00:46:04.900 --> 00:46:06.440
No way...

00:46:07.880 --> 00:46:10.140
You better tell me something at the end of these credits.

00:46:10.140 --> 00:46:13.100
You'd better tell me something at the [frustrated whispering]

00:46:15.220 --> 00:46:18.420
[angry Mark growl]

00:46:18.420 --> 00:46:23.060
[awkward silence]

00:46:23.680 --> 00:46:27.220
Aah, I'm just gonna...[frustrated muttering]

00:46:27.220 --> 00:46:30.060
There has to have been something, there HAS to have been

00:46:30.060 --> 00:46:33.340
something, because I missed...many a thing.

00:46:33.340 --> 00:46:36.180
It doesn't show me all the things that I've missed, here.

00:46:37.040 --> 00:46:37.540
But...

00:46:38.780 --> 00:46:41.100
it does show a lot that I've gotten.

00:46:41.880 --> 00:46:44.300
I got a lot of...

00:46:45.140 --> 00:46:47.860
[mutters] What is this..."Towers of Metal."  This was it.

00:46:47.860 --> 00:46:51.120
"Five miles beyond the mines."

00:46:51.480 --> 00:46:53.160
Beyond the mines, far side of the mountain.

00:46:53.160 --> 00:46:55.700
So, the mines were the closest thing to them.

00:46:56.820 --> 00:47:01.120
Camouflaged metal towers by as- asymmetrical trees...

00:47:01.660 --> 00:47:07.800
"I was overcome with waking dreams as of a power I had never experienced before."

00:47:10.100 --> 00:47:12.140
"There were flames and incense and what have...

00:47:12.140 --> 00:47:15.480
may have been mouths and may have been sex organs."

00:47:15.480 --> 00:47:19.360
It really brings out the base level of the brain.

00:47:19.360 --> 00:47:21.600
The lizard brain.  The base thing.

00:47:21.600 --> 00:47:24.400
You know, it really tramps onto that, and it amplifies it.

00:47:24.400 --> 00:47:27.340
In some way.  And it causes visions and hysteria because there's...

00:47:27.860 --> 00:47:28.780
[frustrated growl]

00:47:29.540 --> 00:47:30.140
I don't know.

00:47:31.360 --> 00:47:31.860
But...

00:47:32.760 --> 00:47:35.300
That's all we have for now.

00:47:35.300 --> 00:47:36.300
Now remember...

00:47:37.080 --> 00:47:40.480
In the original Outlast there was the Whistleblower DLC

00:47:40.480 --> 00:47:43.940
which shed some more light on what was happening

00:47:44.000 --> 00:47:48.620
And in the end the Wallrider seemed like an ethereal thing

00:47:48.620 --> 00:47:50.920
but you know, it was- it was explained in the original Outlast

00:47:50.920 --> 00:47:54.600
and also, you know, in Whistleblower to a greater detail.

00:47:54.600 --> 00:47:58.800
So I would not be surprised if this had more.

00:47:58.800 --> 00:47:59.320
Now...

00:47:59.320 --> 00:48:02.880
All that story aside, I am gonna say about Outlast 2

00:48:02.920 --> 00:48:06.500
the game, from a gameplay standpoint

00:48:06.900 --> 00:48:07.740
[kissing noise]

00:48:08.200 --> 00:48:09.660
I loved that!

00:48:09.660 --> 00:48:10.992
It was different!

00:48:11.000 --> 00:48:14.120
it was definitely different in certain extremes

00:48:14.120 --> 00:48:16.420
about Outlast and the experience of that it was.

00:48:16.420 --> 00:48:19.680
In my opinion, it had just a little bit too much

00:48:19.680 --> 00:48:23.040
of the merry-go-round chasing and running away from people.

00:48:23.180 --> 00:48:27.780
But it had moments...that were just gosh-darn terrifying.

00:48:27.780 --> 00:48:32.620
I actually really liked the flipping in and out of reality aspect of it.

00:48:32.620 --> 00:48:36.200
I think that added a lot of depth to it, and just showed

00:48:36.540 --> 00:48:40.220
How...whatever was in that world was affecting Blake.

00:48:40.220 --> 00:48:43.740
and how his past, and his main source of guilt

00:48:43.740 --> 00:48:46.540
and his entire existence was just brought up.

00:48:48.780 --> 00:48:50.960
And it was amplified, to an extreme degree.

00:48:50.960 --> 00:48:53.920
This was a worthy successor to Outlast

00:48:53.920 --> 00:48:55.740
but not without its flaws.

00:48:55.740 --> 00:48:59.760
And I'm sure someone else could point out its flaws much better than I ever could

00:48:59.760 --> 00:49:01.080
but even so...

00:49:01.460 --> 00:49:07.080
It took the subject matter and it didn't even shy away an inkling to it.

00:49:07.160 --> 00:49:10.320
It went as deep as you could possibly go

00:49:10.320 --> 00:49:13.460
into the perversion, the bloodiness, the goriness

00:49:13.460 --> 00:49:15.500
the horrific nature of this

00:49:15.500 --> 00:49:19.300
It- it didn't skirt around religion, it didn't do ANY of that.

00:49:19.300 --> 00:49:24.240
It hit it head-on, and I can appreciate something that takes itself seriously

00:49:24.240 --> 00:49:26.420
to an extreme degree.

00:49:27.100 --> 00:49:28.400
And that's what this did.

00:49:29.300 --> 00:49:32.080
And I-I, I really really really enjoyed this.

00:49:32.080 --> 00:49:34.660
I did, I LOVED this game.

00:49:35.080 --> 00:49:37.640
I did, I-I...from a- from a gameplay standpoint

00:49:37.640 --> 00:49:41.320
there were flaws and there were story flaws and there's holes, obviously!

00:49:41.320 --> 00:49:42.960
and there's unanswered questions

00:49:42.960 --> 00:49:45.920
but from a pure experience standpoint

00:49:46.120 --> 00:49:48.240
That was flippin' amazing!

00:49:48.860 --> 00:49:50.660
I had a blast! [laughing]

00:49:51.280 --> 00:49:54.360
I was frustrated at times, but I never wanted to stop going!

00:49:54.360 --> 00:49:55.180
But either way...

00:49:55.700 --> 00:49:56.720
I'll leave it at that.

00:49:56.940 --> 00:49:59.480
Let me know what you guys thought of it down in the comments below

00:49:59.480 --> 00:50:01.020
I wanna hear your opinions about this.

00:50:01.020 --> 00:50:03.280
I want to hear your theories about the story.

00:50:03.280 --> 00:50:06.360
I want to know what is possibly going on here

00:50:06.360 --> 00:50:10.880
and how it could in any way relate to the original Outlast.

00:50:10.880 --> 00:50:13.720
Because this wouldn't be Outlast 2

00:50:13.920 --> 00:50:19.540
if there might not be some [whining] tangentially related things.

00:50:20.840 --> 00:50:21.800
But we'll see.

00:50:21.800 --> 00:50:26.060
We'll see what happens in the future and we'll see what gets dug up.

00:50:26.060 --> 00:50:28.760
[outro music starts] So thank you everybody so much for watching

00:50:29.140 --> 00:50:31.560
and as always, I will see YOU...

00:50:31.800 --> 00:50:33.000
in the next video!

00:50:33.820 --> 00:50:34.700
Bye-bye!

00:50:34.700 --> 00:50:40.200
[outro music plays]

